(2t+3{t}^{4}){e}^{{t}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 true] [17592186167328 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165177 13194139535185 17592186045417 false] [17592186177945 1078 #edb/ref 17592186177947 13194139535185 17592186045417 true] [17592186179445 1071 "Calculate $2.4 \\div (-1.2)$." 13194139535185 17592186045417 false] [17592186179445 1071 "Calculate $2.4 \\div (-1.2).$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 true] [17592186179445 1074 "Dividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n2.4\\div 1.2 = 2\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-1.2) = -2\n$$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 false] [17592186179445 1074 "Dividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n2.4\\div 1.2 = 2,\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n2.4 \\div (-1.2) = -2.\n$$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 true] [17592186179446 1071 "Find the value of $\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2)$." 13194139535185 17592186045417 false] [17592186179446 1071 "Find the value of $\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2).$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 true] [17592186179446 1074 "Dividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{4}{7 \\times 2} = \\dfrac{4}{14} = \\dfrac{2}{7}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2) = -\\dfrac {2}{7}\n$$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 false] [17592186179446 1074 "Dividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{4}{7 \\times 2} = \\dfrac{4}{14} = \\dfrac{2}{7},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2) = -\\dfrac {2}{7}.\n$$" 13194139535185 17592186045417 true] [17592186179447 1071 "Find the value of $\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right) \\div \\dfrac{1}{10}$." 13194139535185 17592186045417 false] [17592